elden ring is full of  little things that help immerse you into  its world and being able to sheath your  weapons is one of those  yes this is a very minor thing but it  does make you look a little bit more  presentable in cut scenes or when  talking to npcs and if you're someone  who records footage like me then this is  a very handy tool so to shade your sword  you need to ensure that your offhand is  empty and then you tap triangle and l1  to stash your blade away and most  weapons are simply slung at your side or  over your shoulder but some swords have  these beautiful scabbards that really  are worth showing off the glintstone  chris the banished knights greatsword  and the rivers of blood katana are just  a few examples of weapons that have  detailed scabbards that you'll want to  admire you should always be conscious of  your character's elden bling because you  never know whose world your character  will end up in  remember those random npc characters  that you fought during fears questline  what about the npcs that you fought in  front of the great jar  well a recent discovery has revealed  that these are actually the uploaded  characters of other real players and  there must be millions of options that  the game is actually choosing from  matt gruen on twitter has revealed some  of the incredible workings behind this  system for example if you're online  while getting hugged by fear then your  character's build is allegedly being  uploaded to the elden ring servers and  apparently these saved builds are then  passively loaded while in the deep root  depths that means your character can  actually appear as fierce champion in  another player's game a similar thing  happens when you receive the great jars  arsenal where your character can then  appear as a knight of the great jar in a  different player's world but even if  your character is uploaded matt points  out that it doesn't mean your build will  always be used  we don't yet know the inner workings of  this system there must be some other  requirements to make sure these builds  aren't completely non-functional but  it's so damn cool that elden ring can  pull your build out of its enormous jar  of warriors so to speak  crazy discovery next you'll have noticed  that ruins are a pretty common sight on  your journey through the lands between  thing is these always seem to have  underground areas with treasures or  bosses or two bosses but while most  ruins have obvious entrances to their  underground others conceal them with  planks or even magic so if you find a  ruin without an underground area try  your best to look for an illusory floor  an easy way to spot them is by looking  for a rectangle that doesn't quite blend  in  as you can see here  you can also use the incantation law of  regression which reveals mimicry but an  even better version is the omen shackle  items which are kind of bugged and have  a huge hitbox that can trigger illusory  walls to open  for number 23 there have been some  quality of life updates added in recent  patches as well that are proving pretty  helpful in their own small ways a really  useful one is this small glowing icon  that now appears at the site of grace  menu it indicates that you have flask  upgrades on hand so now you know exactly  when you have enough sacred tears or  golden seeds to craft and upgrade with  for number 24 alongside the flask update  the item description for golden runes  now finally says how many runes you'll  gain from consuming them on their  description page it reads that the rune  is used to gain x amount of runes making  it a much easier way to consume based on  exactly what you need  as far as updates go though redan might  be the boss who's undergone the most  since the game's release the conqueror  of stars is still tough to beat but  there is another way you can approach  this fight that will make it a little  less difficult  so this video from limit breakers shows  that you can actually fully defeat radan  just by using npc summons limit breakers  found that there are 10 banners in the  boss arena and that each one has a  collection of summon signs beneath it  that never changes in total there are 41  summon signs but each one can only be  used once  limit breaker's helpful graphic really  breaks it all down you should go and  watch his video but basically blythe can  be summoned six times as can lionel try  goth and geron although geron only  appears in phase two which i found  interesting because it's basically like  he's only joining in on the fight when  he knows radan is probably going to die  okina and finger maiden therolina can be  summoned five times alexander can be  used three times and patches can be  summoned four times though he kind of  just pieces out immediately if you do  summon him which is hilarious but even  without patches that's 37 fighters which  is basically an army and while it does  take them a while to chip away at  radan's health you can also use buffs  like the commander's standard to help  them out in the end the summons can do  quite a number on the big guy which is  especially relevant if you're under  leveled just be ready for quite a long  battle  in fact while you're riding around  during this long battle why not listen  to some audiobooks this month i'd like  to recommend 1q84 by murakami which you  can listen to completely free just head  over to audible.com varietyvideo or text  variety video to 500 500 and claim your  30-day free audible trial to get full  access to thousands and thousands of all  you can listen audiobooks original  entertainment and podcasts as well  included in the plus catalog  but if you want you can use your free  trial on the murakami book i recommended  and murakami books are pretty legendary  i think everyone should read at least  one they're these stories that are often  grounded in reality but  they have a reality that really starts  to unwind and takes the reader on an  intense journey here's a small excerpt  from 1q84  be careful it looks windy out there  don't slip  i'll be careful aomami said  and also the driver said facing the  mirror  please remember  things are not what they seem  if this sounds good to you then go to  audible.com  or text vaatividia to 500 500 and get  your free trial started today thank you  to audible for sponsoring this video and  thank you for watching
 

